AGENT DESIGNER — Guide Page Writer

Help me build ONE AI agent for my user guide folder. Use plain words, no jargon.

THE AGENT'S JOB
I give the agent a screenshot of the app. It writes one user guide page
for the feature shown in that screenshot.

BEFORE IT STARTS, IT READS THESE IN ORDER:
1. My app design: [design file name, saved in this folder]
   → to understand the app, its screens and its features.
2. SKILL.md
   → to learn the step-by-step process it must follow.
3. Page template: [template file name]
   → to learn the structure every page must follow.
4. Screenshots folder: [folder name]
   → example screenshots it can look at when it needs a reference.

HOW EACH JOB RUNS:
1. I give it a screenshot.
2. It reads the 4 sources above.
3. It finds which screen and feature the screenshot shows, using the design file.
4. It writes the guide page using the page template, following SKILL.md.
5. It checks the page against the template and the design, fixes any gaps
   (max 2 rounds), then gives the page to me.

IT MUST STOP AND ASK ME WHEN:
- It can't tell which screen or feature the screenshot shows.
- The screenshot shows something that isn't in the design file.
- Any of the 4 sources is missing.

Then follow the AGENT DESIGNER steps: look first, ask me up to 3 questions,
show me the plan, build it, wrap up.
